%% Official YD-ESP32-S3 reference design has two different Type-C connectors.
flowchart LR
    APP[Shahbaz Android application]
    ANDROID[Android phone<br/>operational USB Host]
    WIN[Windows PC<br/>development HIL only]
    NATIVE[Native ESP32-S3 USB Type-C<br/>official YD design<br/>GPIO19 D- / GPIO20 D+<br/>Shahbaz operational data link]
    ESP[shahbaz_interface_board<br/>ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8<br/>physical PCB match UNVERIFIED]
    UART[Separate USB-to-UART Type-C<br/>WCH CH343P<br/>programming / diagnostics]
    DEVPC[Development PC]

    APP <--> ANDROID
    ANDROID <--> NATIVE
    WIN -. HIL only .-> NATIVE
    NATIVE <--> ESP
    DEVPC <--> UART
    UART <--> |UART0 GPIO43 / GPIO44| ESP
